      <guid isPermaLink="false">8282f16fb4b79df995320986</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:25:44 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Europe’s power mix is changing fast. Ample output from wind, solar and nuclear means that Northwest Europe could require significantly less power from fossil fuels this winter than last. At the same time, rising electricity demand from EVs and data centers is shifting market dynamics across Europe, creating new opportunities for technologies like solar and batteries. So how are Europe’s power markets evolving, and what does that mean for prices and investment? On today’s show, Tom Rowlands-Rees</description>
